From 4e10629960c603ca60122ebc78d8cef3caace05b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tasker <tasker@localhost>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 23:12:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 28/35] intel-hda-ace: crash-async is armed at the reset too

The machine's reset follows the device's realize and deletes the knob's
timer with the others, so a crash-async set at the device's creation never
fired (the first qtest run of the knob: its timer never called, the debug
line of the reset at the clock's zero). The reset arms it again from its
own time, as the realize does: N ms count from the machine's start for a
knob set at the creation, and from the set for one set while the VM runs.
The first qtest row's "nothing pending after the boot" read the target
register whole, which keeps the acknowledged FW_READY's header: the row
reads the busy bit now (the next commit).
---
 hw/audio/intel-hda-ace.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/audio/intel-hda-ace.c b/hw/audio/intel-hda-ace.c
index b410a9288..db33dd97b 100644
--- a/hw/audio/intel-hda-ace.c
+++ b/hw/audio/intel-hda-ace.c
@@ -2435,6 +2435,10 @@ static void intel_hda_ace_reset(DeviceState *dev)
     timer_del(s->reply_timer);
     timer_del(s->crash_timer);
     s->crash_posted = false;
+    /* the machine's reset follows the realize: a knob set at the creation is armed from here */
+    if (s->crash_timer && s->fault_id == ACE_FAULT_CRASH_ASYNC) {
+        ace_arm(s->crash_timer, (uint64_t)s->fault_arg * 1000000);
+    }
     s->hfdsscs = 0;
     s->dsp2cxctl = 0;
     s->inten = 0;
